  "Number": 17,
  "Question": "If \\(x\\) is positive and \\(\\log x\\ge\\log2+\\dfrac12\\log x,\\) then:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(x\\) has no minimum or maximum value",
    "B": "the maximum value of \\(x\\) is \\(1\\)",
    "C": "the minimum value of \\(x\\) is \\(1\\)",
    "D": "the maximum value of \\(x\\) is \\(4\\)",
    "E": "the minimum value of \\(x\\) is \\(4\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Using the conventional common logarithm, subtract \\(\\frac12\\log x\\) from both sides and multiply by the positive number \\(2\\):\n\\[\n\\frac12\\log x\\ge\\log2,\n\\qquad\n\\log x\\ge2\\log2=\\log4.\n\\]\nThe common logarithm is increasing on positive numbers, so this is equivalent to \\(x\\ge4\\). The value \\(x=4\\) gives equality in the original inequality, so the minimum is attained. Thus the minimum value is \\(\\boxed{4}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
